    differentiation=dict(
        ese="Give the perfect-square and perfect-cube lists from Unit 2's reference sheet and let them stay out; a root is a lookup today, not a recall. On every board with arithmetic under the bar, the student draws a box around the radicand before writing anything, so the grouping is a physical act.",
        ell="Radicand and radical are the two new nouns, and they are easy to confuse because they sound alike. Write √25 once with RADICAL circling the whole symbol and RADICAND labelling only the 25, and point at the labels on every board.",
        enrichment="Ask for a pair of numbers for which √(a + b) really does equal √a + √b, and what has to be true of them. Then ask why the same question for a product has a different answer."),

